Z||000000||RICK||12-11-1999||01:19 PM||||Sorry, but this is non Fiero related, I know a lot of you guys and gals work on all kind of cars so this is the first place I had to turn.  My Dad's 2nd car is a 89 Caviler with the 4cyl, auto, 69k miles. When it's cold it starts every time with no problem, when it gets warmed up sometimes it will just stop running and wont start.  Sometimes after driving it, shutting it off for a couple min. and then trying to restart it, it will not start, the engine turns over but it wont even try and start.  I pulled the codes (using the instructions for the Fiero) and all I would get is code 12 which is ok.  My Dad thanks you for your help.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shiner||12-11-1999||02:22 PM||||What condition is the air filter in?  ||||reg||5
Z||000002||RICK||12-11-1999||03:47 PM||||Air filter is new||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||12-11-1999||04:05 PM||||Since it is a newer car we can rule out vapor lock... which this sounds like.<P>When heat is the problem, it usually points to electrical problems.  Make sure that he is getting enough spark when the engine is hot.  So first check out the electrical.  Make sure that his coil, and spark distribution system are functioning properly, if that is the case then check and see if the plugs and wires are sending the spark to the cylindars.  If that is the case then check fuel pressure.  What sometimes happens is your fuel actually boils in the lines.  As I said before, this is a long shot... a VERY long shot.  It is best to see if he can simulate this no-start problem while checking the pressure.  If it isn't around 15 psi then you have a problem with the fuel delivery system.  ||||reg||3
Z||000004||dogtired||12-12-1999||01:27 AM||||Don't know about a Cavilar, but if it were a Fiero I would suspect either the Coil or Ignition module. Both will breakdown with heat and be intermittent(s/p)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>If that car doesn't have these parts?<P>NEVER MIND  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Good Luck||||reg||6
Z||000005||Monkeyman||12-12-1999||03:45 AM||||My wife has a '98 Cavalier with the same specs so I can tell you exactly what the problem is.  It's a piece of junk!  Ours has been in the shop numerous times.  I told the service mgr that the next time it had to come in the shop it was getting there through the front window.  Check for any recalls.  There were 7 (!) on my wifes car.||||reg||1
